# Input Component v2

## Purpose & Scope

`Input` is a compound component for text input fields in the eToro design system. It provides a flexible, accessible input with:

- **Compound component pattern**: `Input.Label`, `Input.Field`, `Input.TextAdornment`, `Input.IconAdornment` subcomponents
- **Uncontrolled by default**: Uses `defaultValue` instead of `value` for better performance
- **Built-in states**: focus, error, disabled, readonly
- **Password visibility toggle**: Automatically rendered when `type="password"` (no need to include in JSX)
- **Helper text & character counter**: Automatically rendered when `error` exists or `showCharCounter` is true (no need to include in JSX)
- **Floating label animation**: Animated label that floats when focused or filled
- **Context-based state sharing**: No prop drilling, all state shared via React Context

**Does NOT handle:**

- Form validation logic (handle in parent)
- Form submission logic (handle in parent)
- Navigation logic (use with router/navigation handlers)
- Auto-complete/suggestions (use separate components)
- Multi-line text input (use TextArea component instead)

## Entry Points & Contracts

### `Input` (main component - context provider)

```tsx
<Input
  style?: StyleProp<ViewStyle>  // Container style override
  backgroundColor?: string      // Input surface fill override (inside border)
  type?: InputType              // Input type (default: 'text')
  defaultValue?: string         // Initial value for uncontrolled mode
  error?: string | null         // Error message (helper text; border follows focus only)
  disabled?: boolean            // Disabled state (default: false)
  readonly?: boolean            // Read-only state (default: false)
  maxLength?: number            // Maximum character length
  showCharCounter?: boolean     // Shows character counter when maxLength is set (default: false)
  showPasswordToggleWhenDisabled?: boolean // Keeps the eye toggle rendered + tappable while disabled (default: false — disabled password fields hide it)
>
  {children}
</Input>
```

**Children constraints:**

- Must contain `Input.Label` and `Input.Field` at minimum
- Optional: `Input.TextAdornment`, `Input.IconAdornment`
- Password toggle is automatically rendered when `type="password"` - do not include it in JSX
- Helper text is automatically rendered when `error` exists or `showCharCounter` is true - do not include it in JSX
- Order matters for visual layout

### `Input.Label`

```tsx
<Input.Label
  required?: boolean            // Shows asterisk if required
  style?: StyleProp<TextStyle>  // Optional override, merged on top of the DS-driven animated typography (size/lineHeight/letterSpacing/color/fontFamily). Omit for default look.
>
  {string}                      // Label text (e.g., "Label" or "Label(Read only)")
</Input.Label>
```

### `Input.Field`

```tsx
<Input.Field
  onChangeText?: (text: string) => void
  placeholder?: string
  ref?: Ref<TextInput>
  // ...all other TextInput props (except value, onChangeText, defaultValue)
  testID?: string
  accessibilityLabel?: string
  accessibilityHint?: string
/>
```

**Note:** `type`, `disabled`, `readonly`, `maxLength`, and `defaultValue` are set on the `Input` root component, not on `Input.Field`. The `defaultValue` flows from the root component to `Input.Field` via context. The component only supports uncontrolled mode with `defaultValue` - controlled mode with `value` is not supported.

### `Input.TextAdornment`

```tsx
<Input.TextAdornment>{string} // e.g., "Suffix", "USD"</Input.TextAdornment>
```

### `Input.IconAdornment`

```tsx
<Input.IconAdornment
  iconName: IconName            // Required - icon from icon library
  size?: number                 // Default: 20
  color?: string                // Optional color override
  onPress?: () => void          // Optional interaction handler
/>
```

### Types

| Type        | Values                                                           |
| ----------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `InputType` | `'text'` \| `'password'` \| `'email'` \| `'number'` \| `'phone'` |

## Usage Patterns

### Basic input (simplest)

```tsx
<Input defaultValue="">
  <Input.Label>Label</Input.Label>
  <Input.Field onChangeText={setValue} />
</Input>
```

### With character counter

```tsx
<Input type="email" maxLength={50} showCharCounter defaultValue="">
  <Input.Label>Email</Input.Label>
  <Input.Field onChangeText={setEmail} placeholder="your@email.com" />
</Input>
```

### With error state

```tsx
<Input type="password" defaultValue="" error="Password must be at least 8 characters">
  <Input.Label>Password</Input.Label>
  <Input.Field onChangeText={setPassword} />
</Input>
```

**Note:** The password toggle and helper text are automatically rendered when `type="password"` or `error` exists - no need to include them in JSX.

### With text adornment

```tsx
<Input type="number" maxLength={10} showCharCounter defaultValue="">
  <Input.Label>Amount</Input.Label>
  <Input.Field onChangeText={setAmount} placeholder="0.00" />
  <Input.TextAdornment>USD</Input.TextAdornment>
</Input>
```

### With icon adornment

```tsx
<Input defaultValue="">
  <Input.Label>Search</Input.Label>
  <Input.Field onChangeText={setSearch} placeholder="Search..." />
  <Input.IconAdornment iconName="search" />
</Input>
```

### Read-only state

```tsx
<Input readonly defaultValue="1234567890">
  <Input.Label>Account Number</Input.Label>
  <Input.Field />
  <Input.TextAdornment>Read only</Input.TextAdornment>
</Input>
```

## Anti-patterns

### ❌ Using Input outside of Input root

```tsx
// BAD - will throw runtime error
<Input.Field onChangeText={setValue} />

// BAD - will throw runtime error
<Input.Label>Label</Input.Label>
```

**Fix:** Always wrap Input sub-components inside `<Input>`.

### ❌ Using defaultValue on Input.Field instead of Input root

```tsx
// BAD - defaultValue should be on Input root, not Input.Field
<Input>
  <Input.Label>Label</Input.Label>
  <Input.Field defaultValue="value" onChangeText={setValue} />
</Input>
```

**Fix:** Set `defaultValue` on the `Input` root component. It will automatically flow to `Input.Field` via context.

### ❌ Using value prop (controlled mode not supported)

```tsx
// BAD - controlled mode is not supported
<Input defaultValue={name}>
  <Input.Field value={name} onChangeText={setName} />
</Input>
```

**Fix:** Only use `defaultValue` on the `Input` root component for uncontrolled mode. Controlled mode with `value` prop is not supported.

### ❌ Missing required children

```tsx
// BAD - missing Input.Label
<Input defaultValue="">
  <Input.Field onChangeText={setValue} />
</Input>

// BAD - missing Input.Field
<Input defaultValue="">
  <Input.Label>Label</Input.Label>
</Input>
```

**Fix:** Always include both `Input.Label` and `Input.Field` as minimum.

### ❌ Manually styling colors/sizes for no reason

```tsx
// BAD - bypasses design system with no design justification
<Input.Label style={{ color: 'red', fontSize: 20 }}>Label</Input.Label>
```

**Fix:** Use component props and variants. Colors come from theme automatically. `Input.Label`'s `style` prop exists only to match a specific, verified Figma spec that diverges from the default animated variant (e.g. a bespoke typography spec on one screen) — not as a shortcut for arbitrary one-off styling. Always use theme tokens (`colors.*`) for color, never raw hex/named colors.

### ❌ Using showCharCounter without maxLength

```tsx
// BAD - counter won't show without maxLength
<Input showCharCounter defaultValue="">
  <Input.Label>Name</Input.Label>
  <Input.Field onChangeText={setName} />
</Input>
```

**Fix:** Set `maxLength` on `Input` root component for character counter to work.

## Dependencies & Edges

### Internal Dependencies

- `useEtoroTheme` - provides theme colors for styling
- `EtText` - underlying text component for `Input.TextAdornment` and helper text (auto-rendered)
- `EtoroIcon` - underlying icon component for `Input.IconAdornment` and password toggle (automatically rendered)
- Split context architecture (see "Context Architecture" below):
  - `InputConfigContext` - static props (type, disabled, readonly, etc.)
  - `InputStateContext` - interaction state (focus, password visibility, hasValue, animations)
  - `InputValueContext` - current value (hot path, changes on every keystroke)
- `Animated.View` and `Animated.Text` (react-native-reanimated) - used for `Input.Label` with floating animation (View for transform, Text for fontSize)
- `PasswordToggle` - automatically rendered by `Input` root when `type="password"` (not a user-facing component)

### External Dependencies

- `expo-haptics` - haptic feedback on focus and password toggle
- `react-native` - `TextInput`, `View`, `StyleSheet`, `Pressable`
- `react-native-reanimated` - animations for floating label and border color

### Public layout constants

`INPUT_LAYOUT_METRICS`, `INPUT_INNER_HEIGHT`, and `INPUT_COMPACT_LABEL_FIELD_GAP` are exported from the `input-v2` public barrel (`libs/etoro-ui/src/components/input/input-v2/index.ts`). Downstream kit consumers (e.g. EtDatepicker) may import them to share the same box model. Renaming or reshaping these is a breaking public API change.

### Design System Integration

Colors come from theme (`useEtoroTheme().colors`) — V2 tokens, per Figma `49177:4012`:

| Slot                                              | V2 token                              |
| ------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------- |
| Container background (default)                    | `carbon900` at ~5% (`${carbon900}0D`) |
| Container border (idle / unfocused)               | `transparent`                         |
| Container border (focused, non-readonly)          | `carbon600`                           |
| Container border (disabled)                       | `carbon300`                           |
| Floating label (idle large + compact small)       | `carbon500`                           |
| Floating label (disabled)                         | `carbon500`                           |
| Input value text                                  | `carbon900`                           |
| Input value text (disabled, compact)              | `carbon500`                           |
| Placeholder                                       | `carbon400`                           |
| Cursor + selection highlight                      | `primary600`                          |
| Adornment / suffix / icon (idle)                  | `carbon500`                           |
| Adornment / suffix / icon (focused)               | `carbon900`                           |
| Adornment / suffix / icon (disabled)              | `carbon300`                           |
| Password toggle (idle)                            | `carbon500`                           |
| Password toggle (focused)                         | `carbon900`                           |
| Password toggle (disabled)                        | `carbon300`                           |
| Error helper text                                 | `verdictNegative500`                  |

#### Behavior deltas (V1 → V2)

- **Container fill** changes from a solid `bgNeutralGreyPrimary` grey to a `carbon900` overlay at ~5% opacity. Caller-supplied `backgroundColor` prop still wins.
- **Disabled state** no longer dims the entire chrome via `opacity: 0.6`. Instead it renders with full opacity, a static `carbon300` border, `carbon500` for label / value (kept legible), and `carbon300` for adornments / password-toggle.
- **Error helper text** moves from `actionBrandVarText` (`#D12515`) to `verdictNegative500` (`#F55249`) — a per-component decision driven by Figma `49177` (other components in the kit map V1 error to `verdictNegative600`).

### Typography & Spacing

- Typography:
  - Label: `Animated.Text` driven by `useInputAnimations` (idle = `body-base-regular`, compact = `body-tiny-medium`)
  - Helper / Error text: `body-tiny-regular` variant
  - Text adornment: `body-base-regular` variant
- Spacing uses design tokens:
  - Left / right padding: `X4` (16px)
  - Gap between input area and helper text: `X1` (4px)
- Icon sizes default to 20px (configurable)

## Patterns & Pitfalls

### Uncontrolled mode only

The component only supports uncontrolled mode with `defaultValue`. Set `defaultValue` on the `Input` root component (not on `Input.Field`). Controlled mode with `value` prop is not supported. The parent syncs via `onChangeText` callback. This design choice improves performance by avoiding unnecessary re-renders.

### Password toggle auto-rendering

When `Input` root has `type="password"`, the password toggle is automatically rendered by the `Input` component. **Do not include `<Input.PasswordToggle />` in your JSX** - it is not a user-facing subcomponent and will not work if you try to use it.

### Helper text auto-rendering

Helper text is automatically rendered when:

- `error` prop is provided (shows error message in red), OR
- `showCharCounter` is `true` and `maxLength` is set (shows character counter)

**Do not include `<Input.HelperText />` in your JSX** - it is not exported and will not work if you try to use it. The helper text is automatically rendered below the input when needed.

### Error takes precedence

When `error` is provided to `Input`, the error message is shown (red). Character counter is hidden when an error is present.

### Context Architecture

The input uses a **split context pattern** for optimal re-render performance. State is divided into 3 contexts based on update frequency:

| Context              | Contains                                                             | Updates when...              | Hook                    |
| -------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------- | ----------------------- |
| `InputConfigContext` | `type`, `disabled`, `readonly`, `maxLength`, `defaultValue`, `error` | Props change (rare)          | `useInputConfig()`      |
| `InputStateContext`  | `isFocused`, `isPasswordVisible`, `hasValue`, handlers, animations   | Focus, toggle, empty↔filled | `useInputInteraction()` |
| `InputValueContext`  | `currentValue`, `setValue`                                           | Every keystroke (hot path)   | `useInputValue()`       |

**Which hook each component uses:**

| Component        | Hooks Used                                               | Re-renders on typing?                |
| ---------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------ |
| `IconAdornment`  | `useInputConfig`                                         | No                                   |
| `FloatingLabel`  | `useInputInteraction`                                    | No (only on empty↔filled)           |
| `InputField`     | `useInputConfig`, `useInputInteraction`, `useInputValue` | Yes (needs setValue)                 |
| `InputContainer` | `useInputConfig`, `useInputInteraction`                  | No                                   |
| `HelperText`     | `useInputValue`                                          | Yes (needs currentValue for counter) |

**File structure:**

```
context/
├── config-context.tsx   # InputConfigContext + useInputConfig
├── state-context.tsx    # InputStateContext + useInputInteraction
├── value-context.tsx    # InputValueContext + useInputValue
├── input-provider.tsx   # Composed provider (nests all 3)
└── index.ts             # Re-exports hooks and provider
```

**Notes:**

- `showCharCounter` does NOT flow to context - it's passed directly as a prop to `InputContainer` and then to `HelperText`
- `HelperText` uses `useInputValue()` for the character counter

### Read-only state

When `readonly={true}`, the input:

- Is non-editable (`editable={false}`)
- Shows transparent border
- Label shows "(Read only)" text (you should include this in the label text yourself)

### Focus state management

Focus state is managed internally and triggers:

- Label animation (floats up)
- Border color animation (changes to active color)
- Haptic feedback (if enabled)

### Character counter

Character counter only displays when:

- `showCharCounter={true}` on `Input` root component
- `maxLength` is set on `Input` root component
- No error is present (error takes precedence)

The character counter is automatically rendered as part of the helper text component when these conditions are met.

